notes:
These are the primary sources the csoh.org kill chain cites. Every fact about the incident in this deck comes from that page, which draws on these.

Halcyon disclosed the campaign on January 13, 2025, and its post is the first link in the page's header. Arctic Wolf's post on the campaign is the second. The Register covered Codefinger, and the MITRE page defines T1486, Data Encrypted for Impact, behind stage 04.

The three AWS pages back the page's AWS statements: the Security Blog post with the CopyObject pattern AWS describes, which Halcyon says was published in response to its report; the FAQ on the SSE-C default change; and the guide to which S3 calls CloudTrail records by default.

The background slides name their own sources, from AWS documentation and the csoh.org glossary.

